-- title:
--   Sums over idele class characters of K lying above ξ_L
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, write $\iota$ for the map $K^\times \to \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ induced by $K \to \mathbb{A}_K$, and let $N$ be the idelic norm attached to the base change of adele rings along $L/K$, that is, the map on unit groups induced by the $\mathbb{A}_K$-algebra norm $\mathbb{A}_L \to \mathbb{A}_K$ coming from the ring homomorphism $\mathbb{A}_K \to \mathbb{A}_L$ together with the identification $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ compatible with $L \to \mathbb{A}_L$. Let $\xi_L$ be a homomorphism from the full unit group of $\mathbb{A}_L$ (presented as the top subgroup) to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, and let $\Xi$ be a finite set of homomorphisms from the full unit group of $\mathbb{A}_K$ to $\mathbb{C}^\times$, assumed to consist of exactly those $\xi$ such that $z \mapsto \xi(z) \in \mathbb{C}$ is continuous on $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$, $\xi$ is trivial on the range of $\iota$, and $\xi(N z) = \xi_L(z)$ for all $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$. Then: (1) for all $a \in K^\times$ and $z \in \mathbb{A}_L^\times$, $\sum_{\xi \in \Xi} \xi(\iota(a) \cdot N z) = |\Xi| \cdot \xi_L(z)$ in $\mathbb{C}$; (2) for every $u \in \mathbb{A}_K^\times$ outside the subgroup generated by the ranges of $\iota$ and of $N$, $\sum_{\xi \in \Xi} \xi(u) = 0$; (3) if $\Xi$ is nonempty, then $|\Xi|$ equals the index of that subgroup in $\mathbb{A}_K^\times$.
--
--   This is the character-theoretic bookkeeping used in base change for $\mathrm{GL}(2)$: the set of idele class characters of $K$ restricting to a prescribed character $\xi_L$ along the norm is a coset of the character group of the norm residue group $\mathbb{A}_K^\times / K^\times N(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)$, which is finite because $K^\times N(\mathbb{A}_L^\times)$ is open of finite index; openness of the norm range enters through [`NumberField.isOpen_range_idelicNorm`](thm.html#NumberField.isOpen_range_idelicNorm). It is used downstream to convert integrals over fundamental domains into integrals of functions composed with the idelic norm, and in the comparison of elliptic terms for automorphic forms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_NumberField_sum_ideleClassChar_eq_of_comp_idelicNorm_eq.lean

